# [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_CLI] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]

CLI entry: parse flags, validate targets, run probes, print report, exit.

## MAIN

<!-- [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_CLI] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]: wires parse, probe, report, and exit code -->

Contract:
  INPUT: command-line arguments
  OUTPUT: exit 0 or 1
  PRE: command-line arguments present
  POST: exit 0 when all probes OK; exit 1 on usage error or any non-OK probe
  EFFECTS: writes report to stdout; usage/validation errors to stderr
  FAILURE_MODES: usage error (exit 1); invalid target (exit 1); non-positive timeout (exit 1); any non-OK probe (exit 1)
  MESSAGE_CONTRACT: N/A — no message/event delivery
  RETRY: N/A — single probe pass per invocation
  IDEMPOTENCY: N/A — operator may re-run; no deduplication obligation
  TERMINATION: total

procedure MAIN(): # [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_CLI] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]
1. PARSE -timeout flag (default 3s)
2. IF no positional targets THEN print usage to stderr and exit 1
3. FOR each positional arg validate host:port format
4. IF timeout <= 0 THEN print error to stderr and exit 1
5. results := RUN_ALL(root context without cancel, targets, timeout, defaultDialFn)
6. print FORMAT_LINES(results) to stdout
7. IF any result status != OK THEN exit 1 ELSE exit 0
